So what I love about this idea is it suggests that we can learn to tolerate effort as a general thing. And the reason for that is because the feeling of effort is a generalized feeling. Yes, when I try hard on my piano, of course, there's something strictly attached to the piano and the finger movements and what have you, but the experience of effort is common. These feelings transfer, and then if we can learn that these feelings signal reward is coming, you then become industrious. I understand that you yourself have absorbed the lesson of your research,
